    <data name="AboutLede" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Northside Market started as one shop on Phibsborough Road in 1998. It's six shops now, all north of the Liffey, and still a family business.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="FrontsTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Our six shops and the year each one opened</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>One oven, the same growers</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryBody1" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Siobhán Byrne opened the first shop with her brother Ciarán, a bread oven in the back room and vegetables from growers in Rush and Lusk, half an hour up the coast.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryBody2" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>The oven still bakes for all six shops before seven every morning, and most of the growers are the same families. A new shop only opens where the bakery can get to it before the doors do.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryBody3" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>What changed is the queue. Since the app arrived in 2024, about a third of our customers order ahead and collect on the way home, and the tills are quieter for everyone else.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="TeamTitle" xml:space="preserve">
